{"type": "message", "id": "ddb30c17", "parentId": "a86d966b", "timestamp": "2026-04-13T04:21:05.634Z", "message": {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "call_c1f20060de3e41eaa54d9c", "toolName": "web_search", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\n  \"query\": \"EPA Carbon Monoxide AQI Portland Vancouver Hillsboro OR WA Wichita KS San Diego Carlsbad CA 2000-2010 all days Good range <=4.4 ppm\",\n  \"provider\": \"brave\",\n  \"count\": 5,\n  \"tookMs\": 1020,\n  \"externalContent\": {\n    \"untrusted\": true,\n    \"source\": \"web_search\",\n    \"provider\": \"brave\",\n    \"wrapped\": true\n  },\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"1318c5c864e18dee\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nAir Quality Index (AQI) Basics\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"1318c5c864e18dee\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.airnow.gov/aqi/aqi-basics/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c860d6578033a669\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThink of the AQI as a yardstick that runs from 0 to 500. The higher the AQI value, the greater the level of air pollution and the greater the health concern. For example, <strong>an AQI value of 50 or below represents good air quality</strong>, while an AQI value over 300 represents hazardous air quality.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"c860d6578033a669\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.airnow.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a88b2cccfe0f11f8\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nAir Quality Criteria For Carbon Monoxide {draft}\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a88b2cccfe0f11f8\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://nepis.epa.gov/Exe/ZyNET.exe/20008EMP.txt?Back=ZyActionS&BackDesc=&Client=EPA&DefSeekPage=&Display=hpfrw&Docs=&EndTime=&ExtQFieldOp=0&File=D:%5CZYFILES%5CINDEX+DATA%5C86THRU90%5CTXT%5C00000005%5C20008EMP.txt&FuzzyDegree=-1&ImageQuality=r85g16/r85g16/x150y150g16/i500&Index=1986+Thru+1990&IntQFieldOp=0&MaximumDocuments=0&Password=anonymous&QField=&QFieldDay=&QFieldMonth=&QFieldYear=&Query=fname%3D%2220008EMP.TXT%22&SearchBack=ZyActionE&SearchMethod=&SortMethod=&Time=&Toc=&TocEntry=&TocRestrict=&UseQField=&User=ANONYMOUS&XmlQuery=&ZyActionW=Download\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"5216f07eaec9a720\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nEmissions and Concentrations of Carbon Monoxide Current air quality standards define <strong>1-hour and 8-hour average concentrations that should not be exceeded more than once per year</strong>. The 1-hour standard of 35 ppm is almost never exceeded in data reported from fixed-site monitoring stations.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"5216f07eaec9a720\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"nepis.epa.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"93a9e746b70bc9aa\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n2021 Oregon Annual Ambient Criteria Pollutant Air Monitoring Network Plan\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"93a9e746b70bc9aa\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://downloads.regulations.gov/EPA-R10-OAR-2022-0124-0017/content.pdf\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"e4f22548c5c1707d\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nEPA has · provided a GC/MS and will provide funds through the PM2.5 grant to purchase a ceilometer and an NO2 · analyzer. DEQ plans to renovate the NCore site with a new shelter to accommodate the added equipment. Delays in construction contracting and budget and staffing constraints will delay PAMS being operational by ... The Portland –Vancouver- Hillsboro CBSA has over 2.5 million people in 2020, triggering the requirement\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"e4f22548c5c1707d\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"downloads.regulations.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"af05bffffabb11d9\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n2017 Oregon Annual Ambient Criteria Pollutant Air Monitoring Network Plan\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"af05bffffabb11d9\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.epa.gov/sites/default/files/2017-11/documents/orplan2017.pdf\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"488c17ef519a126a\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nTable A 3. Carbon Monoxide Minimum Monitoring Requirements: ... EPA requires NO2 near roadway monitoring in CBSAs above 500,000. The monitoring is to be next to a freeway at a location with the highest · annual average daily traffic and highest heavy duty diesel traffic. Portland-Vancouver is the only CBSA in Oregon required to have near road NO2\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"488c17ef519a126a\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.epa.gov\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"cf27e08ab465d1fc\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nAirNow.gov\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"cf27e08ab465d1fc\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://www.airnow.gov/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"790a9423b55ef93f\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n&lt;div class=&quot;tippy-close-holder&quot;&gt;&lt;div onmousedown=&quot;document.activeElement.style.visibility=&amp;apos;hidden&amp;apos;;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;fa fa-times&quot; style=&quot;left:5px;position:absolute;top:5px;z-index:-1;&quot; id=&quot;close-box&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;padding-top:5px;&quot; id=&quot;Map Info Icon Content from Home Current AQ Band&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;This map shows current air quality (&lt;a href=&quot;/aqi/aqi-basics/using-air-quality-index#current-aqi&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Current AQI&lt;/a&gt;) for ozone or PM, whichever is highest.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"790a9423b55ef93f\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"www.airnow.gov\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"}], "details": {"query": "EPA Carbon Monoxide AQI Portland Vancouver Hil